-- title:
--   Ramification index read on the valuation ring S_P
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be Dedekind domains, $F$ a field, with $S$ an $R$-algebra whose underlying $R$-module is torsion-free, and $F$ a fraction field of $S$. Let $p$ be an ideal of $R$ with $p \neq \bot$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a maximal ideal of $S$ lying over $p$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $F$ subject to three conditions: the image of every $s \in S$ under $S \to F$ lies in $P$; for every $s \in S$ the image of $s$ lies in the non-units of $P$ if and only if $s \in \mathfrak P$ (so $P$ is centred on $\mathfrak P$); and every element $e$ of $P$ can be written as a fraction, i.e. there are $s, t \in S$ with $t \notin \mathfrak P$ and $e \cdot \iota(t) = \iota(s)$ for $\iota : S \to F$. Finally let $\varphi : R \to P$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $P \subseteq F$ agrees with $R \to S \to F$. The conclusion is that the ideal of $P$ generated by the image of $p$ under $\varphi$ equals the maximal ideal of the local ring $P$ raised to the power $e(\mathfrak P \mid p)$, the ramification index of $\mathfrak P$ over $p$.
--
--   This is the standard comparison of the ramification index $e(\mathfrak P \mid p)$ with the exponent obtained after localising at $\mathfrak P$ (Serre, Local Fields, I §4): in the factorisation $pS = \mathfrak P^{e}\mathfrak a$ with $\mathfrak a$ coprime to $\mathfrak P$, passing to $S_{\mathfrak P}$ discards $\mathfrak a$ and turns $\mathfrak P$ into the maximal ideal. It is used to transport ramification data from ideals of a Dedekind domain to a valuation subring of the fraction field, in the computation of inertia and of ramification along valuations of the function field of a modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_map_valuationSubring_eq_maximalIdeal_pow_ramificationIdx.lean

import Mathlib

